.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
These functions configure the set of \fBreference identifiers\fR that an
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM\fR will match against the names asserted by a peer\*(Aqs
certificate during certificate verification. Four families of reference
identifier are supported, each matched against a distinct location in the
certificate:
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBDNS hostnames\fR, matched against \fBdNSName\fR entries in the certificate\*(Aqs
subject alternative name (SAN) extension.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBRFC 822 email addresses\fR, matched against \fBrfc822Name\fR entries in the
certificate\*(Aqs SAN.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBSMTPUTF8 email addresses\fR, matched against \fBotherName\fR entries of type
\&\fBid\-on\-SmtpUTF8Mailbox\fR (RFC 8398) in the certificate\*(Aqs SAN.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBIP addresses\fR, matched against \fBiPAddress\fR entries in the certificate\*(Aqs
SAN.
.PP
For each family the \f(CW\*(C`set1_\*(C'\fR form clears any previously configured values
and installs the supplied value as the sole reference identifier, and the
\&\f(CW\*(C`add1_\*(C'\fR form appends the supplied value to the existing list. When a list contains more than
one entry, the certificate is considered to match if any of the configured
values matches a corresponding name in the certificate.
.PP
For the functions whose value is a string with an explicit length (the
hostname and email families), if the length argument is zero
the value must be NUL\-terminated; otherwise the length argument must be the
length of the value in bytes.
.SS "Hostname matching"
.IX Subsection "Hostname matching"
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_host()\fR sets in \fIparam\fR the expected DNS hostname to
\&\fIname\fR, for matching against \fBdNSName\fR SAN entries in the peer\*(Aqs
certificate, clearing any previously specified hostname. If \fIname\fR is NULL
or the empty string, the host list is cleared, hostname matching is
disabled, and the call succeeds.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_host()\fR adds \fIname\fR as an additional reference
identifier that can match a \fBdNSName\fR SAN entry in the peer\*(Aqs certificate.
Any previous names set via \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_host()\fR or
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_host()\fR are retained. If \fIname\fR is NULL or the empty
string, the list is left unchanged and the call succeeds.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get0_host()\fR returns the \fIidx\fRth DNS hostname previously
configured on \fIparam\fR via \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_host()\fR or
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_host()\fR, or NULL if \fIidx\fR is out of range. To iterate
over the configured hostnames, start with \fIidx\fR = 0 and increment \fIidx\fR
until the function returns NULL. The returned string is owned by the library
and remains valid until \fIparam\fR is modified or freed; the caller must
not free it.
.PP
Hostname matching is governed by the \fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_*\fR host flags;
see \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set_hostflags\fR\|(3) for the available flags and
their effect on wildcards and subject\-DN consultation. The names by which
the peer matched can be retrieved via \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get0_peername\fR\|(3).
.SS "Email matching"
.IX Subsection "Email matching"
The \f(CW_rfc822()\fR family of functions is used for email names that have
ASCII localpart addresses, in which case the domain part of the address
must be represented in A\-label form. They are used to specify the list of
values to match against the SAN \fBrfc822Name\fR entries in certificates.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_rfc822()\fR clears all expected RFC 822 email
addresses, and sets the expected RFC 822 email address to \fIemail\fR for
matching against \fBrfc822Name\fR SAN entries in the peer\*(Aqs certificate. A NULL
\&\fIemail\fR clears the RFC 822 list and returns success; the empty string
clears the list but returns failure.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_rfc822()\fR adds \fIemail\fR as an additional reference
identifier that can match a \fBrfc822Name\fR SAN entry in the peer\*(Aqs
certificate. Any previous names set via \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_rfc822()\fR,
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_rfc822()\fR, or \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_email()\fR are
retained on success; no change is made on failure. \fIemail\fR must not be
NULL, and the empty string is rejected as a failure.
.PP
The \f(CW_smtputf8()\fR family of functions is used for email names that have a
non\-ASCII localpart, in which case the domain part of the address must be
represented in U\-label form. They are used to specify the list of values
to match against the \fBotherName\fR entries of type
\&\fBid\-on\-SmtpUTF8Mailbox\fR (RFC 8398) in certificates.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_smtputf8()\fR sets the expected SMTPUTF8 email address
to \fIemail\fR for matching against \fBotherName\fR SAN entries of type
\&\fBid\-on\-SmtpUTF8Mailbox\fR, clearing any previously specified SMTPUTF8 email
address. A NULL \fIemail\fR clears the SMTPUTF8 list and returns success; the
empty string clears the list but returns failure.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_smtputf8()\fR adds \fIemail\fR as an additional reference
identifier that can match an \fBotherName\fR SAN entry of type
\&\fBid\-on\-SmtpUTF8Mailbox\fR in the peer\*(Aqs certificate. Any previous names set
via \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_smtputf8()\fR, \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_smtputf8()\fR,
or \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_email()\fR are retained on success; no change is
made on failure. \fIemail\fR must not be NULL, and the empty string is
rejected as a failure.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_email()\fR is a convenience function that calls
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_rfc822()\fR and \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_smtputf8()\fR with
the same \fIemail\fR argument and succeeds if either call succeeds. This
allows a caller that does not know whether a given email value is
ASCII\-localpart or SMTPUTF8 to install it for matching against both
\&\fBrfc822Name\fR and \fBotherName\fR id\-on\-SmtpUTF8Mailbox SAN entries. A NULL
\&\fIemail\fR clears both lists and returns success.
.PP
When any email address is configured, certificate verification
automatically invokes \fBX509_check_email\fR\|(3). The peer is considered
verified when any one of the specified RFC 822 names matches an
\&\fBrfc822Name\fR SAN entry, or any one of the specified SMTPUTF8 names
matches an \fBotherName\fR id\-on\-SmtpUTF8Mailbox SAN entry, in the
certificate.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get0_email()\fR returns a previously configured expected
email address from \fIparam\fR, or NULL if neither an RFC 822 nor an
SMTPUTF8 address has been set. When both have been configured, the first
RFC 822 address is returned in preference to any SMTPUTF8 address. The
returned string is owned by the library and remains valid until \fIparam\fR
is modified or freed; the caller must not free it.
.SS "IP address matching"
.IX Subsection "IP address matching"
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_ip()\fR sets the expected IP address to \fIip\fR for
matching against \fBiPAddress\fR SAN entries in the peer\*(Aqs certificate,
clearing any previously specified IP address. The \fIip\fR argument must be
in binary format, in network byte order, and \fIiplen\fR must be 4 for IPv4
or 16 for IPv6. A NULL \fIip\fR clears the IP list, disables IP matching, and
returns success.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_ip()\fR adds \fIip\fR as an additional reference
identifier that can match an \fBiPAddress\fR SAN entry in the peer\*(Aqs
certificate. Any previous addresses set via \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_ip()\fR,
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_ip()\fR, \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_ip_asc()\fR, or
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_ip_asc()\fR are retained on success; no change is
made on failure. It is a failure if \fIip\fR is NULL or \fIiplen\fR is neither
4 nor 16.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_ip_asc()\fR sets the expected IP address to \fIip_asc\fR
for matching against \fBiPAddress\fR SAN entries in the peer\*(Aqs certificate,
clearing any previously specified IP address. The \fIip_asc\fR argument
must be a NUL\-terminated ASCII string: dotted decimal quad for IPv4 and
colon\-separated hexadecimal for IPv6. The condensed "::" notation is
supported for IPv6 addresses. A NULL \fIip_asc\fR clears the IP list and
returns success; a string that cannot be parsed as an IP address, including
the empty string, returns failure and leaves the list unchanged.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_ip_asc()\fR adds \fIip_asc\fR as an additional reference
identifier that can match an \fBiPAddress\fR SAN entry in the peer\*(Aqs
certificate. The format requirements on \fIip_asc\fR are the same as for
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_ip_asc()\fR. Any previous addresses set via
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_ip()\fR, \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_ip()\fR,
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_ip_asc()\fR, or \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add1_ip_asc()\fR are
retained on success; no change is made on failure. \fIip_asc\fR must not be
NULL; a string that cannot be parsed as an IP address, including the empty
string, is a failure.
.PP
When any IP address is configured, certificate verification automatically
invokes \fBX509_check_ip\fR\|(3) to match against \fBiPAddress\fR SAN entries.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get1_ip_asc()\fR returns a previously configured expected
IP address from \fIparam\fR as a freshly allocated ASCII string (dotted
decimal quad for IPv4, colon\-separated hexadecimal for IPv6), or NULL if
no IP address has been set. The caller is responsible for freeing the
returned string with \fBOPENSSL_free\fR\|(3).
.SS "Input validation"
.IX Subsection "Input validation"
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_host_input_validation()\fR,
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_rfc822_input_validation()\fR,
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_smtputf8_input_validation()\fR and
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set1_ip_input_validation()\fR install a caller\-supplied
callback that validates a reference\-identifier value at the point it is
configured via the corresponding \f(CW\*(C`set1_\*(C'\fR or \f(CW\*(C`add1_\*(C'\fR function. The
callback receives the value and its length, and returns a nonzero value to
accept the input or zero to reject it; on rejection the \f(CW\*(C`set1_\*(C'\fR/\f(CW\*(C`add1_\*(C'\fR
call fails and no value is stored.
.PP
These callbacks override OpenSSL\*(Aqs built\-in input validation for the
corresponding name type. They affect only the validation performed when
reference identifiers are installed on the verification parameters; they
do not affect the actual matching performed during certificate
verification.
.SH "RETURN VALUES"
.IX Header "RETURN VALUES"
The \f(CW\*(C`set1_\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`add1_\*(C'\fR functions return 1 for success and 0 for
failure.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get0_host()\fR and \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get0_email()\fR return
a pointer to a library\-owned string, or NULL if no such configured value
exists (\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get0_host()\fR also returns NULL when its index
argument is out of range). Callers must not free the returned pointer.
.PP
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get1_ip_asc()\fR returns a freshly allocated string that
the caller must free with \fBOPENSSL_free\fR\|(3), or NULL if no IP address
has been configured.
.PP
The \f(CW\*(C`set1_*_input_validation()\*(C'\fR functions do not return a value.
.SH NOTES
.IX Header "NOTES"
The reference identifier lists configured by these functions are
consulted by \fBX509_verify_cert\fR\|(3) when the corresponding \fBX509_check_*\fR
checks are performed. Configuring a list for a given name type implicitly
enables the corresponding check; clearing it (by passing NULL or the
empty string to the \f(CW\*(C`set1_\*(C'\fR form) disables it.
.PP
By default only the subject alternative name extension is consulted. When
\&\fBX509_CHECK_FLAG_ALWAYS_CHECK_SUBJECT\fR is set, the configured hostnames
are also matched against the \fBcommonName\fR attribute of the certificate\*(Aqs
subject distinguished name, and the configured RFC 822 email addresses
against the subject \fBemailAddress\fR attribute. SMTPUTF8 email and IP
addresses have no subject distinguished name counterpart and are always
matched only against the subject alternative name extension. See
\&\fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_set_hostflags\fR\|(3) and \fBX509_check_host\fR\|(3).
